## Non-negotiable constraints to remind the agent of during implementation

- No method's `extract()` implementation may block the dispatch pool
  indefinitely — subprocess calls always get a timeout.
- Never overwrite or mutate a `ResultEntry` once appended.
- Never hardcode a method's output fields into the dashboard/output layer —
  always go through the YAML-declared schema + `kind`.
- Do not add a new output `kind` to satisfy one method; reuse the existing
  four unless there's a genuine structural need.
- Keep the capture source, session correlator, and method dispatch as three
  separable components at all times — a live-vs-pcap switch, or an
  eBPF-vs-libpcap capture backend, should never require touching dispatch or
  method code.